---
title: Turkish Red Lentil Soup
description: Red lentils and a little rice simmered until they break down, finished with Aleppo pepper oil.
tags: [soup]
course: main
icons: [bowl-hot, pepper-hot, citrus]
cuisine: Turkish
difficulty: easy
source:
  name: Milk Street
  book: Tuesday Nights
  url: https://katu.com/amnw/am-northwest-cooking-recipes/milk-street-turkish-red-lentil-soup
servings: 4
time: 45m
---

In a large #saucepan{} over medium heat, melt the @salted butter{3%tbsp}. Once it stops foaming, add the @yellow onion{1}(medium, cut into 1/2-inch dice, about 1 cup) and cook, stirring, until softened and translucent, about ~soften{5%minutes}.

> **Swaps** — For a vegan soup, use olive oil in place of the butter.

Add the @garlic clove{1}(medium, finely grated) and cook until fragrant, ~cook{30%seconds}.

Add the @tomato paste{1%tbsp}, @sweet paprika{1%tbsp} and @ground cumin{1/2%tsp} and cook, stirring, for ~toast{1%minute}.

Add the @red lentils{1%cup}, @long-grain white rice{2%tbsp}, @water{5%cup} and @kosher salt{2%tsp}(plus more to taste) and bring to a boil. Adjust the heat to hold a lively simmer, cover, and cook until the lentils and rice are tender and broken down, about ~simmer{30%minutes}. Taste and season with salt.

Meanwhile, in a small #skillet{} over medium heat, heat the @extra-virgin olive oil{3%tbsp}, swirling to coat the pan. Add the @Aleppo pepper{2%tsp} and cook until a few bubbles appear and the oil turns bright red. Remove from the heat and set aside.

> **Swaps** — No Aleppo pepper? Use an additional 1 tsp sweet paprika and 1/2 tsp red pepper flakes.

Ladle the soup into bowls and drizzle the Aleppo pepper oil over each serving. Serve with @?fresh mint{}(chopped) and @lemon wedges{}.
